- **Tests:** unit tests in `#[cfg(test)] mod tests` at the end of the source file (apps/browser/src/about_pages.rs:200-201; apps/browser/src/browser_history.rs:166-167; apps/browser/src/favicon.rs:70-72; apps/browser/src/url_suggestions.rs:339-340; apps/browser/persistence/src/lib.rs:310-311; packages/blitz-dom/src/net.rs:609-610; packages/blitz-dom/src/mutator.rs:1566-1567; packages/blitz-dom/src/document.rs:3188-3189; packages/blitz-dom/src/stylo_to_parley.rs:525-526; packages/blitz-dom/src/util.rs:180-181; packages/blitz-dom/src/node/scrollbar.rs:224-237; packages/blitz-dom/src/node/element.rs:1081-1215; packages/blitz-dom/src/node/node.rs:2084-2170; wpt/runner/src/test_runners/fuzzy.rs:138-140; wpt/runner/src/test_runners/js_wrapper.rs:106-108; wpt/runner/src/test_runners/harness_test.rs:286-292; wpt/runner/src/test_runners/mod.rs:402-404); eight unit-test modules sit in files of their own, each a `#[cfg(test)]` child declared through `#[path]` at its parent — dioxus-native-dom's bridge tests, declared at the end of `dioxus_document.rs` as `#[cfg(test)] #[path = "dioxus_document_tests.rs"] mod bridge_tests;`, a child of the module under test so they reach its private fields with no constructor, `pub` or `cfg(test)` shim added (packages/dioxus-native-dom/src/dioxus_document.rs:834-836), and, since 2026-10-16-file-splits, blitz-dom's `document::changed_set_tests` and `document::font_reading_tests` in `document_changed_set_tests.rs` and `document_font_reading_tests.rs` (packages/blitz-dom/src/document.rs:3763-3765; packages/blitz-dom/src/document.rs:3767-3769) and escher-driver's `mcp::tests` and `schema::tests` in `mcp_tests.rs` and `schema_tests.rs` (packages/escher-driver/src/mcp.rs:291-293; packages/escher-driver/src/schema.rs:543-545), each moved out whole with its test paths unchanged;
 each integration test file covers one behavior and opens with a `//!` doc naming the behavior and any guarded bug (tests/blitz-tests/tests/anonymous_block_leak.rs:1-7; tests/blitz-tests/tests/comment_layout.rs:1-7); regression tests cite upstream issue or PR URLs (tests/blitz-tests/tests/animations.rs:4; tests/blitz-tests/tests/render_blocking_stylesheet.rs:1; tests/blitz-tests/tests/stale_interaction_state.rs:5; tests/blitz-tests/tests/stale_node_mapping.rs:2; tests/blitz-tests/tests/custom_widget_layout.rs:3); documents built with `HtmlDocument::from_html` and a `DocumentConfig` with a `ColorScheme::Light` viewport and `HtmlProvider`, then `resolve(0.0)` (tests/blitz-tests/tests/accessibility_hidden.rs:139-145; tests/blitz-tests/tests/comment_layout.rs:14-25); scenarios run in both layout modes `for incremental in [false, true]` (tests/blitz-tests/tests/anonymous_block_cache_invalidation.rs:92-101; tests/blitz-tests/tests/flex_grid_order.rs:85-99); descriptive snake_case test names (tests/blitz-tests/tests/dir_attribute.rs:32; tests/blitz-tests/tests/dir_attribute.rs:39); `#[track_caller]` assertion helpers (tests/blitz-tests/tests/accessibility_roles.rs:40-41); some tests use `test_that` matchers returning `TestResult<()>` (tests/blitz-tests/tests/accessibility_hidden.rs:6; tests/blitz-tests/tests/accessibility_hidden.rs:9-25); a pointer-event builder is repeated per file (tests/blitz-tests/tests/details_element.rs:43-62; tests/blitz-tests/tests/fragment_navigation.rs:45-64;
 tests/blitz-tests/tests/scrollbar_drag.rs:13-32), while the seven_guis stand checks state the tables and helpers they share once, in the module `tests/blitz-tests/tests/common/mod.rs`, which a check reads by declaring `mod common;` — a module in a subdirectory of the integration-test directory is no test target, so each test-target file still covers one behavior (tests/blitz-tests/tests/common/mod.rs:1-6) — and the checks that hold a `Session` — the session checks, the settle check `stand_settle`, the fifteen driver-action checks `stand_act_*`, since 2026-10-10-mcp-surface `stand_mcp_tools`, since 2026-10-12-headless-screenshot, `stand_screenshot_repeat` and, since 2026-10-14-stand-requirement-sweep, the driver sweep `stand_requirement_sweep`, and the served-page checks `stand_cells_served` and `stand_load_page` — keep what they share in a second such module, `tests/blitz-tests/tests/session_common/mod.rs`, read by `mod session_common;` (tests/blitz-tests/tests/session_common/mod.rs:1-7); tests first assert the fixture produces the condition under test (tests/blitz-tests/tests/anonymous_block_leak.rs:50-55; tests/blitz-tests/tests/interaction_state_canonicalization.rs:76-91); WPT test names use forward slashes relative to WPT_DIR (wpt/runner/src/main.rs:621-625); the CI Python tests use `unittest` with one `TestCase` per function (.github/scripts/test_wpt_diff_to_pr.py:4; .github/scripts/test_wpt_diff_to_pr.py:104-174); blitz-tests keeps one test target per file directly under `tests/` — its `[package]` sets no `autotests` — and the one file there that is declared and never built is upstream's single-binary `tests/all.rs`, the manifest's one `[[test]]` table, held at `test = false`: the operator's decision of 2026-10-10, a standing two-line difference from upstream's manifest that `BlitzTestsTargetsTest` pins (tests/blitz-tests/Cargo.toml:46-59; .github/scripts/test_blitz_tests_targets.py:17-26)
